        "text": "‘Chandrabindu - The Woven Moon’ takes inspiration from Kumar Purnima, where the full moon is worshipped as a symbol of purity and fortune. Reimagined in the Dhalapathar Parda, the moon becomes a bold central motif, with crescents, waves, and star-like butis woven through the extra-weft. A palette of deep indigo with ivory and silver mirrors moonlight on a night sky, turning the parda into a poetic “sky-window” that unites festival, cosmos, and craft.",
